[h1]MdsBuildTools: grid snapping, alignment & floor fix (open-source mod, beta)[/h1]

Hey everyone! Like a lot of you in the [i]Grid Snapping[/i] threads, I kept fighting with furniture that wouldn't line up, and objects sinking into the floor. So I built a free, open-source mod to fix that.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Grid snapping[/b]: position snaps to a grid (default 5 cm) and scroll rotation to steps (default 15°) instead of the fixed 45°. Both are configurable and work on walls too.
[*][b]Alignment[/b]: edges and centres line up with nearby furniture automatically.
[*][b]Keep above floor[/b]: objects that sink into the floor get pushed back up onto the surface.
[/list]

[h2]Every feature can be toggled[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]G[/b]: grid snapping on/off
[*][b]H[/b]: alignment on/off
[*][b]J[/b]: floor fix on/off
[*]Hold [b]Left Alt[/b]: place freely (no snapping or alignment) while held
[/list]
All keys can be rebound. If you have [b]ModSettingsAPI[/b] installed there's also an in-game settings tab, and otherwise there's a config file.

[h2]Status[/h2]
[b]Beta.[/b] Everything is hooked into the game, but it's freshly made, so expect rough edges. If something acts weird, toggle that feature off with its hotkey and post your [i]BepInEx/LogOutput.log[/i] here or on GitHub.

[b]Exact wall lengths[/b] (no more 1 m walls) are next. The room editor is built on a fixed 1 m grid, so it's a bigger job and I'm doing it as a separate opt-in feature.

[h2]Install[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Install BepInExPack via [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/my-dream-setup/]Thunderstore[/url] (r2modman or Gale)
[*](Optional) Install ModSettingsAPI for the in-game menu
[*]Drop [i]MdsBuildTools.dll[/i] into [i]BepInEx/plugins[/i]
[/olist]

[h2]Source / downloads[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/miguelneves01/MdsBuildTools]github.com/miguelneves01/MdsBuildTools[/url] (MIT licence)

Feedback welcome! What other building tools would you want? Exact wall lengths are already on the list. A measuring tape? Copy/paste with exact offsets? Let me know below.

[i]Not affiliated with the developers. Mods are used at your own risk, so back up your saves.[/i]
